comments.body:
we can use the same fix as I metion in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/143008#issuecomment-3677398247

```diff
diff --git a/Modules/_io/textio.c b/Modules/_io/textio.c
index f988195256..6bcf9877e8 100644
--- a/Modules/_io/textio.c
+++ b/Modules/_io/textio.c
@@ -2644,6 +2644,7 @@ _io_TextIOWrapper_seek_impl(textio *self, PyObject *cookieObj, int whence)
     posobj = PyLong_FromOff_t(cookie.start_pos);
     if (posobj == NULL)
         goto fail;
+    CHECK_ATTACHED(self);
     res = PyObject_CallMethodOneArg(self->buffer, &_Py_ID(seek), posobj);
     Py_DECREF(posobj);
     if (res == NULL)
@@ -2965,12 +2966,11 @@ static PyObject *
 _io_TextIOWrapper_truncate_impl(textio *self, PyObject *pos)
 /*[clinic end generated code: output=90ec2afb9bb7745f input=8bddb320834c93ee]*/
 {
-    CHECK_ATTACHED(self)

     if (_PyFile_Flush((PyObject *)self) < 0) {
         return NULL;
     }
-
+    CHECK_ATTACHED(self)
     return PyObject_CallMethodOneArg(self->buffer, &_Py_ID(truncate), pos);
 }
 ```

I think when call PyObject_CallMethodOneArg we check the `CHECK_ATTACHED` before that, can avoid these problem?

@jackfromeast what do you think
